-- title:
--   Recursive regional data of the released global candidate
-- statement:
--   Recursive regional data below the released global stage of the exact More Asymmetry seed: for each of the six level-3 regions, the 88 positive terms present in it with their parent grade triples (in step coordinates, where step mode j is physical mode roles rho j), block counts, split masses and complete level-2 word histograms; and the pooled level-2 region with its 1104 positive terms, in physical coordinates. All values are read off the published exact seed, and counts are per unit of the global scale.
-- source:
--   Alman-Duan-Vassilevska Williams-Xu-Xu-Zhou, More Asymmetry Yields Faster Matrix Multiplication (https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.16349), sections 5-6, applied to the published exact seed of the released parameters. Data only; no claim is made here.

import Definitions.Def_mme_released_global_joint_counts
import Definitions.Def_mme_recursive_yz_physical_words
open BigOperators MME MME.RecursiveYZ MME.MoreAsymmetryExactSeed
set_option autoImplicit false
set_option maxRecDepth 100000
namespace MME.ReleasedRecursive

/-! Recursive regional data of the released exact seed, below its global stage.

Level three: six regions (orientations); region `ρ` hashes all 88 positive terms present in it,
in step coordinates where step mode `j` is physical mode `roles ρ j`. Level two: one pooled region
over the 1104 positive level-2 terms `(term, ρ, shape)`, in physical coordinates. Counts are per
unit of the global scale `k` (a global block count `denominator^5 * k` per owner). -/

def emptyTerm : Term := ⟨[], [], [], [], [], [], []⟩

def seedTerm (o s : ℕ) : Term := ([owner0, owner1, owner2, owner3, owner4, owner5].getD o []).getD s emptyTerm

def galphaAt (o s : ℕ) : ℕ := (globalAlpha.getD o []).getD s 0

